        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "An example of the kind of work [Catherine de Medici] appreciated is the Museum's panel of yellow satin embroidered with silk threads. One of a set of three (the others are in the Musée Historique des Tissus, Lyon), it hung as a valence around the top of a four-poster bed. Various print sources were culled for the airy design of grotesques, while its five vignettes derived from Ovid's Metamorphoses- based on the myths of Europa, Actaeon, Semele, Pyramus, and Salmacis- are adapted from woodcut illustrations published by Bernard Salomon in Lyon in 1557. Its brilliant colors, exquisite design, and sumptuous material would have suited the queen's taste perfectly."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/50844d3e-c3d3-3b27-ae84-4cfc39e0fe82> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/8d46fa18-b66d-31df-b0a9-241846ed4ee1> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c4a5ce91-e386-3c6c-81f9-6eebdc60335f> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/5665c39b-077c-3c5f-ad7a-1ea2aa8bc6bf> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/6d1b2e2e-3cbb-33de-a5d1-9c2a1c1a0014> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/651c3a9a-9c23-3e1d-b81c-eb31d655ad19> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/deb14853-4c52-3201-ac1d-26f2738384aa> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "An example of the kind of work [Catherine de Medici] appreciated is the Museum's panel of yellow satin embroidered with silk threads. One of a set of three (the others are in the Musée Historique des Tissus, Lyon), it hung as a valence around the top of a four-poster bed. Various print sources were culled for the airy design of grotesques, while its five vignettes derived from Ovid's Metamorphoses- based on the myths of Europa, Actaeon, Semele, Pyramus, and Salmacis- are adapted from woodcut illustrations published by Bernard Salomon in Lyon in 1557. Its brilliant colors, exquisite design, and sumptuous material would have suited the queen's taste perfectly."@en ;
